# These files are compiled into the binary verbatim with `include_str!`.
# Normalize their bytes across platforms so a Windows package advertises the
# same resources, ships the same legal text, and parses the same data as the
# macOS and Linux packages built from the same commit.
#
# Without this, Git converts them to CRLF on a Windows checkout and every one
# of them is embedded with different bytes there. The rule used to name only
# `docs/skills/**/SKILL.md`, which left the rest of the set converted; a test
# asserting on a line break inside `docs/mcp-security-model.md` is what found
# the gap. Anything new reached by `include_str!` belongs in this list.
#
# The catch-all below is what makes that instruction survive being forgotten.
# Naming each file one at a time is exactly the rule that was already
# incomplete twice: seven `include_str!` targets — this repository's own Rust
# sources among them, which several tests scan as text — were still being
# converted after the list was extended the first time. `* text=auto` puts
# every text file in the repository on LF in the index, so a new
# `include_str!` is normalized before anyone remembers to add a line here.
# The explicit entries stay: they are the set whose bytes reach a package,
# and `eol=lf` states it for them even where a future `.gitattributes` edit
# narrows the default.
* text=auto eol=lf
docs/mcp-server-instructions.md text eol=lf
docs/mcp-security-model.md text eol=lf
docs/policy-authoring.md text eol=lf
docs/skills/**/SKILL.md text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md text eol=lf
contrib/polkit/com.ekubo.wallet.policy text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/networks.json text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/default-tokens.json text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/token-prices.json text eol=lf
crates/mcp-bridge/src/offline_capabilities.json text eol=lf
schemas/policy.schema.json text eol=lf
assets/app-icon.svg text eol=lf
# Rust sources are reached by `include_str!` too, and read as text by the
# tests that scan a module for its own shape rather than running it.
src/desktop.rs text eol=lf
src/release_check.rs text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/src/policy_store.rs text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/src/reconcile.rs text eol=lf
crates/ekubo-wallet-core/src/update_trust.rs text eol=lf
